@startuml
!theme plain

participant "Central site" as Central
actor Browser
participant "Remote site (SP)" as Remote
participant IdP

Central -> Remote : activate changes:\n   connection list, ACS URL, certificates

Browser -> Remote : GET <REMOTE>/check_mk/login.py
Remote --> Browser : login form with one button per\n   connection listed for this site

Browser -> Remote : GET <REMOTE>/check_mk/saml_sso.py\n   RelayState="<saml_connection_id>,index.py"
Remote -> Remote : connection listed for this site?\n   (and customer allowed?)
Remote --> Browser : (form to be auto-submitted to IdP)\n   SAMLRequest signed with the\n   propagated key material

Browser -> IdP : POST <SingleSignOnService Location>\n   RelayState,SAMLRequest
IdP --> Browser : (form to be auto-submitted to SP)\n   SAMLResponse with\n   Recipient=<REMOTE ACS>

Browser -> Remote : POST <REMOTE>/check_mk/saml_acs.py?acs\n   RelayState,SAMLResponse
Remote -> Remote : validate SAMLResponse\n   Recipient == own ACS endpoint\n   create or update the user
Remote --> Browser : 302 Redirect\n   Set-Cookie: auth_REMOTE="..."

@enduml
